      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Louis Armstrong (1901–1971) transformed jazz from New Orleans collective improvisation into virtuoso solo trumpet and vocal art."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "recordings",
      "title": "Recordings",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Hot Five and Hot Seven sessions (1920s) set templates for swing, blues inflection, and improvising on changes. *West End Blues* opening cadenza remains iconic."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "swing",
      "title": "Swing",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Rhythmic feel placing emphasis flexibly within the beat — not metronomic equality. 'Playing behind the beat' then catching up."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "storytelling",
      "title": "Storytelling",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Simple start, build intensity, memorable ending — applies to variation on the repeat in dance music."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
